  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Tuesday...\n\nWarm and mostly dry conditions continue into the first half of the\nday, with high temperatures mostly in the 70s and 80s. Winds will\nincrease by this afternoon out of the southwest ahead of the \nfirst piece of a complex system sliding into the region. Expect to\nsee widespread gusts of 25 to 40 mph east of Billings and 40 to \n55 mph from Billings west. Currently, there is a 40% chance of a \ngust greater than 60 mph over the Absaroka/Beartooth foothills \nthis afternoon and evening. With these warm, dry, and breezy\nconditions, elevated grass fire concerns continue.\n\nAs the first piece of the system moves in, the chance for\nprecipitation will begin to increase from west to east this\nafternoon and evening, bringing snow over the mountains and rain\nover the plains. Enough instability will accompany this wave for a\nfew weak thunderstorms to develop, with the main threat being\ngusty and erratic winds. Precip accumulations with this first\nround will remain mostly light outside of the mountains, with \ngenerally a less than 20% chance of at least 0.1\" through midnight.\n\nBy Thursday morning, the first piece of the system will begin to\nslide northeast into Canada, bringing a 50-80% chance of precip to\nlocations east of Billings. The second piece of the system then\ndrops south, pushing a cold front through the region. High temps\nwill be much cooler than the first half of the week, falling to\nupper 40s to low 50s Thursday and mostly 40s Friday. Winds will \nincrease with the front and turn out of the northwest. Expect to \nsee widespread gusts in the 40s and 50s through the day Thursday, \nwith a 20-30% chance for some gusts greater than 60 mph.\n\nThe second piece of the system merges with the first piece\nThursday afternoon. This upper low then wraps precip around over \nthe region. The mountains and foothills will be favored due to \nupslope enhancement, allowing periods of mountain snow to continue\nthrough the day Friday. The mountains have a 60-80% chance of at\nleast 8\" of snow through Friday. Over the immediate foothills, \nthere is a 40-60% chance of at least 4\" of snow. Occasional light\nsnow showers remain possible (20-50% chance) over the plains, \nalthough there will be little to no snow accumulations, with \ngenerally a less than 20% chance of more than 1\" of snow.\n\nConditions remain unsettled into early next week, keeping temps\ncooler and allowing occasional light rain and snow showers. \nArcher",
